{"code":"it","name":"Italian","native":"Italiano","phase":1,"medium":"en","file_level":"A2","level":{"title":"Elementary: city, travel, routines, health","goals":["Find your way around an Italian city","Talk about past trips with passato prossimo","Describe routines, health, and future plans"],"units":[{"id":"A2-U1","title":"Getting around","lessons":[{"id":"A2-U1-L1","title":"Around the city (a Roma, in Italia)","learn":"Cities take A, countries take IN: VADO A ROMA (I go to Rome), VADO IN ITALIA (I go to Italy). Location uses STARE: STO A CASA (I am at home). Sinistra (left), destra (right), sempre dritto (straight)!","vocab":[{"t":"la strada","r":"lah STRAH-dah","en":"street","pos":"noun"},{"t":"la piazza","r":"lah PYAHT-tsah","en":"square","pos":"noun"},{"t":"la stazione","r":"lah stah-TSYOH-neh","en":"station","pos":"noun"},{"t":"la banca","r":"lah BAHN-kah","en":"bank","pos":"noun"},{"t":"l'ospedale","r":"loh-speh-DAH-leh","en":"hospital","pos":"noun"},{"t":"il negozio","r":"eel neh-GOH-tsyoh","en":"shop","pos":"noun"},{"t":"la sinistra","r":"lah see-NEE-strah","en":"left","pos":"noun"},{"t":"la destra","r":"lah DEH-strah","en":"right","pos":"noun"}],"grammar":{"title":"A + city · IN + country","explain":"VADO A ROMA (city), VADO IN ITALIA (country). STO A CASA (at home). Big places take IN, dots on the map take A!","pattern":"a + city · in + country · sto/stai/sta + place","examples":[{"t":"Vado a Roma.","r":"VAH-doh ah ROH-mah.","en":"I go to Rome."},{"t":"Vado in Italia.","r":"VAH-doh een ee-TAH-lyah.","en":"I go to Italy."},{"t":"Sto a casa.","r":"stoh ah KAH-zah.","en":"I am at home."}],"mistakes":["Saying VADO IN ROMA — cities take A: A ROMA.","Saying VADO A ITALIA — countries take IN: IN ITALIA."]},"dialogue":[{"sp":"Marco","t":"Scusi, dov'è la stazione?","r":"SKOO-zee, doh-VEH lah stah-TSYOH-neh?","en":"Excuse me, where is the station?"},{"sp":"Sofia","t":"È lì, a destra.","r":"eh lee, ah DEH-strah.","en":"It is over there, on the right."},{"sp":"Marco","t":"È lontano?","r":"eh lohn-TAH-noh?","en":"Is it far?"},{"sp":"Sofia","t":"No, è vicino. Cinque minuti.","r":"noh, eh vee-CHEE-noh. CHEEN-kweh mee-NOO-tee.","en":"No, it is near. Five minutes."}],"practice":[{"type":"translate_en","q":"Say: Where is the station?","answer":"Dov'è la stazione?"},{"type":"fill","q":"Vado ___ Roma. (to)","answer":"a"},{"type":"choose","q":"'It is near' is…","options":["È lontano","È vicino","Sto vicino","Sono vicino"],"answer":"È vicino"},{"type":"reorder","q":"Order: Roma / vado / a","answer":"vado a Roma"},{"type":"speak","q":"Say aloud: Dov'è la banca?","answer":"Dov'è la banca?"}],"quiz":[{"q":"VADO A ROMA means…","options":["I am in Rome","I go to Rome","my Rome is big","I like Rome"],"answer":1,"why":"Vado + a = go to."},{"q":"A DESTRA is…","options":["left","right","straight","back"],"answer":1,"why":"Destra = right."},{"q":"Countries take…","options":["a","in","di","da"],"answer":1,"why":"In Italia — big places."},{"q":"DOV'È LA STAZIONE? means…","options":["Who is at the station?","Where is the station?","How is the station?","What is a station?"],"answer":1,"why":"Dov'è = where is."},{"q":"CINQUE MINUTI is…","options":["five minutes","ten minutes","five hours","five days"],"answer":0,"why":"Cinque = 5."}],"flashcards":"auto:vocab","worksheet":{"title":"City worksheet","tasks":[{"instruction":"Translate to Italian.","items":["street","station","shop"],"key":["la strada","la stazione","il negozio"]},{"instruction":"A or IN?","items":["Vado ___ Roma (city)","Vado ___ Italia (country)","Sto ___ casa (home)"],"key":["a","in","a"]},{"instruction":"Ask for directions.","items":["Where is the bank?","Is it far?"],"key":["Dov'è la banca?","È lontano?"]}]}},{"id":"A2-U1-L2","title":"Travel and passato prossimo","learn":"Past trips: HO VISITATO (I visited). Passato prossimo = AVERE (ho, hai, ha) + past verb (visitATO, mangiATO, vedUTO). -ARE verbs just add ATO!","vocab":[{"t":"il viaggio","r":"eel VYAHD-joh","en":"trip","pos":"noun"},{"t":"l'aereo","r":"lah-EH-reh-oh","en":"plane","pos":"noun"},{"t":"l'hotel","r":"LOH-tel","en":"hotel","pos":"noun"},{"t":"la valigia","r":"lah vah-LEE-jah","en":"suitcase","pos":"noun"},{"t":"il biglietto","r":"eel bee-LYEHT-toh","en":"ticket","pos":"noun"},{"t":"la spiaggia","r":"lah SPYAHD-jah","en":"beach","pos":"noun"},{"t":"la montagna","r":"lah mohn-TAHN-yah","en":"mountain","pos":"noun"},{"t":"la foto","r":"lah FOH-toh","en":"photo","pos":"noun"}],"grammar":{"title":"Passato prossimo: ho visitato","explain":"HO + visitATO = I visited. HAI + mangiATO = you ate. HA + vedUTO = he/she saw. Most past verbs end ATO (from -ARE), UTO (-ERE), ITO (-IRE).","pattern":"ho/hai/ha + past verb (ato/uto/ito)","examples":[{"t":"Ho viaggiato in Spagna.","r":"oh vyahd-JAH-toh een SPAHN-yah.","en":"I travelled in Spain."},{"t":"Hai comprato i biglietti?","r":"EH-ee kohm-PRAH-toh ee bee-LYEHT-tee?","en":"Did you buy tickets?"},{"t":"È arrivata ieri.","r":"eh ahr-ree-VAH-tah YEH-ree.","en":"She arrived yesterday. (essere verb!)"}],"mistakes":["Saying HO VIAGGIARE — past needs VIAGGIATO, not the infinitive.","Forgetting movement verbs use ESSERE: È ARRIVATA (she arrived)."]},"dialogue":[{"sp":"Sofia","t":"Hai viaggiato quest'estate?","r":"EH-ee vyahd-JAH-toh kweh-STEH-stah-teh","en":"Did you travel this summer?"},{"sp":"Marco","t":"Sì, ho viaggiato in Messico. Ho visitato la spiaggia.","r":"see, oh vyahd-JAH-toh een MEHS-see-koh. oh vee-zee-TAH-toh lah SPYAHD-jah.","en":"Yes, I travelled in Mexico. I visited the beach."},{"sp":"Sofia","t":"Ti è piaciuto?","r":"tee eh pyah-CHOO-toh?","en":"Did you like it?"},{"sp":"Marco","t":"Mi è piaciuto molto!","r":"mee eh pyah-CHOO-toh MOHL-toh!","en":"I liked it a lot!"}],"practice":[{"type":"translate_en","q":"Say: I travelled in Spain","answer":"Ho viaggiato in Spagna"},{"type":"fill","q":"Hai comprato i ___? (tickets)","answer":"biglietti"},{"type":"choose","q":"'She arrived yesterday' uses…","options":["ha arrivato","è arrivata","arriva","arrivata ha"],"answer":"è arrivata"},{"type":"reorder","q":"Order: visitato / ho / spiaggia / la","answer":"ho visitato la spiaggia"},{"type":"speak","q":"Say aloud: Ho viaggiato in Messico.","answer":"Ho viaggiato in Messico."}],"quiz":[{"q":"HO VISITATO means…","options":["I visit","I visited","you visited","he visits"],"answer":1,"why":"Ho + ATO = I did (past)."},{"q":"LA VALIGIA is…","options":["ticket","suitcase","hotel","beach"],"answer":1,"why":"Valigia = suitcase."},{"q":"TI È PIACIUTO? means…","options":["Did you like it?","Do you like it?","Will you like it?","You like it!"],"answer":0,"why":"Past: did it please you."},{"q":"Which is 'you bought'?","options":["ho comprato","hai comprato","ha comprato","comprare"],"answer":1,"why":"Hai + ATO = you did."},{"q":"IERI means…","options":["tomorrow","today","yesterday","now"],"answer":2,"why":"Ieri = yesterday."}],"flashcards":"auto:vocab","worksheet":{"title":"Travel worksheet","tasks":[{"instruction":"Translate to Italian.","items":["trip","ticket","beach"],"key":["il viaggio","il biglietto","la spiaggia"]},{"instruction":"Put VIAGGIARE in passato prossimo.","items":["I travelled","you travelled","she travelled"],"key":["ho viaggiato","hai viaggiato","ha viaggiato"]},{"instruction":"Answer about a trip.","items":["Did you travel? (yes)","Where? (Mexico)"],"key":["Sì, ho viaggiato","Ho viaggiato in Messico"]}]}}]},{"id":"A2-U2","title":"Life and plans","lessons":[{"id":"A2-U2-L1","title":"Daily routines (reflexive verbs)","learn":"Routines bounce back: MI ALZO = I get (myself) up. MI = myself, TI = yourself, SI = himself/herself. Mornings run on MI/TI/SI: alzarsi, lavarsi, vestirsi!","vocab":[{"t":"la mattina","r":"lah maht-TEE-nah","en":"morning","pos":"noun"},{"t":"il pomeriggio","r":"eel poh-meh-REED-joh","en":"afternoon","pos":"noun"},{"t":"la sera","r":"lah SEH-rah","en":"evening","pos":"noun"},{"t":"il lavoro","r":"eel lah-VOH-roh","en":"work / job","pos":"noun"},{"t":"la scuola","r":"lah SKWOH-lah","en":"school","pos":"noun"},{"t":"la doccia","r":"lah DOHT-chah","en":"shower","pos":"noun"},{"t":"la colazione","r":"lah koh-lah-TSYOH-neh","en":"breakfast","pos":"noun"},{"t":"la cena","r":"lah CHEH-nah","en":"dinner","pos":"noun"}],"grammar":{"title":"Reflexive MI/TI/SI: mi alzo","explain":"ALZARSI = to get up. MI ALZO, TI ALZI, SI ALZA. The little word points back at the person — never drop it!","pattern":"mi/ti/si + verb","examples":[{"t":"Mi alzo alle sette.","r":"mee AHLT-soh AHL-leh SEHT-teh.","en":"I get up at seven."},{"t":"Ti lavi la mattina?","r":"tee LAH-vee lah maht-TEE-nah?","en":"Do you wash in the morning?"},{"t":"Si veste tardi.","r":"see VEH-steh TAHR-dee.","en":"He/She gets dressed late."}],"mistakes":["Saying ALZO without MI — it means 'I lift', not 'I get up'!","Mixing TI and SI: TI = you, SI = he/she."]},"dialogue":[{"sp":"Marco","t":"A che ora ti alzi?","r":"ah keh OH-rah tee AHLT-see?","en":"What time do you get up?"},{"sp":"Sofia","t":"Mi alzo alle sette e faccio la doccia.","r":"mee AHLT-soh AHL-leh SEHT-teh eh FAHT-choh lah DOHT-chah.","en":"I get up at seven and shower."},{"sp":"Marco","t":"E fai colazione?","r":"eh FEH-ee koh-lah-TSYOH-neh?","en":"And do you eat breakfast?"},{"sp":"Sofia","t":"Sì, con la mia famiglia.","r":"see, kohn lah MEE-ah fah-MEE-lyah.","en":"Yes, with my family."}],"practice":[{"type":"translate_en","q":"Say: I get up at seven","answer":"Mi alzo alle sette"},{"type":"fill","q":"Ti ___? (wash)","answer":"lavi"},{"type":"choose","q":"'She gets dressed late' uses…","options":["mi vesto","ti vesti","si veste","ci vestiamo"],"answer":"si veste"},{"type":"reorder","q":"Order: alzo / mi / sette / alle","answer":"mi alzo alle sette"},{"type":"speak","q":"Say aloud: Mi alzo alle sette.","answer":"Mi alzo alle sette."}],"quiz":[{"q":"MI ALZO means…","options":["I lift it","I get up","I sit down","I run"],"answer":1,"why":"Alzo + MI = I get myself up."},{"q":"LA CENA is…","options":["breakfast","lunch","dinner","snack"],"answer":2,"why":"Cena = dinner."},{"q":"A CHE ORA…? asks about…","options":["price","time","place","reason"],"answer":1,"why":"A che ora = at what time."},{"q":"TI LAVI means…","options":["I wash","you wash","she washes","we wash"],"answer":1,"why":"TI = you."},{"q":"Which is reflexive?","options":["parlo","mi chiamo","mangio","vivo"],"answer":1,"why":"Mi chiamo = I call myself."}],"flashcards":"auto:vocab","worksheet":{"title":"Routines worksheet","tasks":[{"instruction":"Translate to Italian.","items":["morning","school","dinner"],"key":["la mattina","la scuola","la cena"]},{"instruction":"Complete with mi, ti, or si.","items":["___ alzo (I)","___ lavi? (you)","___ veste (she)"],"key":["Mi","Ti","Si"]},{"instruction":"Describe your morning.","items":["I get up at …","I shower"],"key":["Mi alzo alle …","Faccio la doccia"]}]}},{"id":"A2-U2-L2","title":"Health and future plans","learn":"At the doctor: MI FA MALE LA TESTA = my head hurts. For plans, Italians use the PRESENT + time word: PARTO DOMANI = I leave tomorrow (I am leaving tomorrow). Simple and natural!","vocab":[{"t":"la testa","r":"lah TEH-stah","en":"head","pos":"noun"},{"t":"la mano","r":"lah MAH-noh","en":"hand","pos":"noun"},{"t":"l'occhio","r":"LOHK-kyoh","en":"eye","pos":"noun"},{"t":"il medico","r":"eel MEH-dee-koh","en":"doctor","pos":"noun"},{"t":"la farmacia","r":"lah fahr-mah-CHEE-ah","en":"pharmacy","pos":"noun"},{"t":"il dolore","r":"eel doh-LOH-reh","en":"pain","pos":"noun"},{"t":"la febbre","r":"lah FEHB-breh","en":"fever","pos":"noun"},{"t":"la salute","r":"lah sah-LOO-teh","en":"health","pos":"noun"}],"grammar":{"title":"Near future: present + time word","explain":"PARTO DOMANI = I leave tomorrow. STUDI STASERA? = Are you studying tonight? Present tense + domani/stasera/lunedì = instant future. (Real futuro comes at B1!)","pattern":"present verb + domani/stasera/…","examples":[{"t":"Parto domani.","r":"PAHR-toh doh-MAH-nee.","en":"I leave tomorrow."},{"t":"Studi stasera?","r":"STOO-dee stah-SEH-rah?","en":"Are you studying tonight?"},{"t":"Piove domani.","r":"PYOH-veh doh-MAH-nee.","en":"It rains tomorrow."}],"mistakes":["Skipping the time word: PARTO alone = I leave (now?).","Using future endings too early — present + domani first!"]},"dialogue":[{"sp":"Marco","t":"Dottore, mi fa male la testa.","r":"doht-TOH-reh, mee fah MAH-leh lah TEH-stah.","en":"Doctor, my head hurts."},{"sp":"Sofia","t":"Hai la febbre?","r":"EH-ee lah FEHB-breh?","en":"Do you have a fever?"},{"sp":"Marco","t":"No, ma riposo domani.","r":"noh, mah ree-POH-zoh doh-MAH-nee.","en":"No, but I rest tomorrow."},{"sp":"Sofia","t":"Bene. Starai bene.","r":"BEH-neh. stah-REH-ee BEH-neh.","en":"Good. You will be fine."}],"practice":[{"type":"translate_en","q":"Say: I leave tomorrow","answer":"Parto domani"},{"type":"fill","q":"Mi fa male la ___. (head)","answer":"testa"},{"type":"choose","q":"'Are you studying tonight?' is…","options":["Studi stasera?","Parto stasera?","Studiare stasera?","Stasera studio io?"],"answer":"Studi stasera?"},{"type":"reorder","q":"Order: domani / parto","answer":"parto domani"},{"type":"speak","q":"Say aloud: Mi fa male la testa.","answer":"Mi fa male la testa."}],"quiz":[{"q":"PARTO DOMANI means…","options":["I left yesterday","I leave tomorrow","I travel now","I want travel"],"answer":1,"why":"Present + domani = plan."},{"q":"MI FA MALE LA TESTA means…","options":["my head hurts","my hand hurts","my eye hurts","my leg hurts"],"answer":0,"why":"Testa = head."},{"q":"LA FARMACIA is…","options":["hospital","pharmacy","clinic","shop"],"answer":1,"why":"Farmacia = pharmacy."},{"q":"STARAI BENE means…","options":["you were fine","you will be fine","you feel bad","you look fine"],"answer":1,"why":"Starai = you will be."},{"q":"Near future needs…","options":["new endings","present + time word","past tense","subjunctive"],"answer":1,"why":"Parto DOMANI — time word!"}],"flashcards":"auto:vocab","worksheet":{"title":"Health worksheet","tasks":[{"instruction":"Translate to Italian.","items":["head","doctor","fever"],"key":["la testa","il medico","la febbre"]},{"instruction":"Write the plan.","items":["I rest tomorrow","You will be fine"],"key":["Riposo domani","Starai bene"]},{"instruction":"At the doctor.","items":["My head hurts","I have a fever"],"key":["Mi fa male la testa","Ho la febbre"]}]}}]},{"id":"A2-U3","title":"Shopping and weather","lessons":[{"id":"A2-U3-L1","title":"Clothes and shopping (questo/quello)","learn":"Shop in Italian! LA CAMICIA, LE SCARPE. Point with QUESTO (this, near me) and QUELLO (that, over there): QUESTA CAMICIA (this shirt), QUEL NEGOZIO (that shop).","vocab":[{"t":"la camicia","r":"lah kah-MEE-chah","en":"shirt","pos":"noun"},{"t":"i pantaloni","r":"ee pahn-tah-LOH-nee","en":"trousers","pos":"noun"},{"t":"le scarpe","r":"leh SKAHR-peh","en":"shoes","pos":"noun"},{"t":"il vestito","r":"eel veh-STEE-toh","en":"dress","pos":"noun"},{"t":"il negozio","r":"eel neh-GOH-tsyoh","en":"shop","pos":"noun"},{"t":"il prezzo","r":"eel PREHD-dzoh","en":"price","pos":"noun"},{"t":"economico","r":"eh-koh-NOH-mee-koh","en":"cheap","pos":"adjective"},{"t":"caro","r":"KAH-roh","en":"expensive","pos":"adjective"}],"grammar":{"title":"QUESTO vs QUELLO: this vs that","explain":"QUESTO/QUESTA = this (near me). QUELLO/QUELLA = that (far). QUELLO shortens like articles: QUEL vestito, QUELLA borsa, QUEI pantaloni, QUELLE scarpe.","pattern":"questo/a + near · quel… + far","examples":[{"t":"Questa camicia è economica.","r":"KWEH-stah kah-MEE-chah eh eh-koh-NOH-mee-kah.","en":"This shirt is cheap."},{"t":"Quel vestito è caro.","r":"kwel veh-STEE-toh eh KAH-roh.","en":"That dress is expensive."},{"t":"Quanto costa questo?","r":"KWAHN-toh KOH-stah KWEH-stoh?","en":"How much is this one?"}],"mistakes":["Saying QUESTO camicia — feminine: QUESTA camicia.","Saying QUELLO vestito — shorten it: QUEL vestito."]},"dialogue":[{"sp":"Marco","t":"Quanto costa questa camicia?","r":"KWAHN-toh KOH-stah KWEH-stah kah-MEE-chah?","en":"How much is this shirt?"},{"sp":"Sofia","t":"Venti euro. È economica.","r":"VEHN-tee eh-OO-roh. eh eh-koh-NOH-mee-kah.","en":"Twenty euros. It is cheap."},{"sp":"Marco","t":"E quel vestito?","r":"eh kwel veh-STEE-toh?","en":"And that dress?"},{"sp":"Sofia","t":"Cinquanta euro.","r":"cheen-KWAHN-tah eh-OO-roh.","en":"Fifty euros."}],"practice":[{"type":"translate_en","q":"Say: This shirt is cheap","answer":"Questa camicia è economica"},{"type":"fill","q":"___ vestito è caro. (that)","answer":"Quel"},{"type":"choose","q":"'That dress is expensive' is…","options":["Questo vestito è caro","Quel vestito è caro","Questa vestita è cara","Quel vestita è caro"],"answer":"Quel vestito è caro"},{"type":"reorder","q":"Order: camicia / economica / è / questa","answer":"questa camicia è economica"},{"type":"speak","q":"Say aloud: Quanto costa questa camicia?","answer":"Quanto costa questa camicia?"}],"quiz":[{"q":"QUESTA CAMICIA means…","options":["that shirt","this shirt","those shirts","my shirt"],"answer":1,"why":"Questa = this (feminine)."},{"q":"I PANTALONI are…","options":["shoes","trousers","shirts","dresses"],"answer":1,"why":"Pantaloni = trousers."},{"q":"QUANTO COSTA…? asks about…","options":["size","price","colour","place"],"answer":1,"why":"Costa = it costs."},{"q":"QUELLO shortens to QUEL before…","options":["feminine nouns","masculine nouns","plurals","verbs"],"answer":1,"why":"Quel vestito — like articles."},{"q":"ECONOMICO means…","options":["expensive","cheap","big","new"],"answer":1,"why":"Economico = cheap."}],"flashcards":"auto:vocab","worksheet":{"title":"Shopping worksheet","tasks":[{"instruction":"Translate to Italian.","items":["shirt","shoes","cheap"],"key":["la camicia","le scarpe","economico"]},{"instruction":"Choose questo, questa, quel, or quella.","items":["___ camicia (this)","___ vestito (that)","___ borsa (that, bag)"],"key":["questa","quel","quella"]},{"instruction":"Ask prices.","items":["How much is this shirt?","How much is that dress?"],"key":["Quanto costa questa camicia?","Quanto costa quel vestito?"]}]}},{"id":"A2-U3-L2","title":"Weather scenes (faceva, c'era)","learn":"Weather stories use IMPERFETTO: FACEVA BELLO (it was nice), C'ERA VENTO (there was wind). Just two phrases paint any past sky!","vocab":[{"t":"il sole","r":"eel SOH-leh","en":"sun","pos":"noun"},{"t":"la pioggia","r":"lah PYOHD-jah","en":"rain","pos":"noun"},{"t":"il freddo","r":"eel FREHD-doh","en":"cold","pos":"noun"},{"t":"il caldo","r":"eel KAHL-doh","en":"heat","pos":"noun"},{"t":"l'estate","r":"leh-STAH-teh","en":"summer","pos":"noun"},{"t":"l'inverno","r":"leen-VEHR-noh","en":"winter","pos":"noun"},{"t":"la nuvola","r":"lah NOO-voh-lah","en":"cloud","pos":"noun"},{"t":"il vento","r":"eel VEHN-toh","en":"wind","pos":"noun"}],"grammar":{"title":"First imperfetto: faceva, c'era","explain":"FACEVA BELLO/FREDDO/CALDO = it was nice/cold/hot. C'ERA + noun = there was…: C'ERA IL SOLE (there was sun). Weather past = imperfetto, always!","pattern":"faceva + weather · c'era + thing","examples":[{"t":"Faceva bello.","r":"fah-CHEH-vah BEHL-loh.","en":"It was nice."},{"t":"C'era vento.","r":"CHEH-rah VEHN-toh.","en":"There was wind."},{"t":"Faceva freddo ieri.","r":"fah-CHEH-vah FREHD-doh YEH-ree.","en":"It was cold yesterday."}],"mistakes":["Saying HA FATTO BELLO for scenes — weather stories use FACEVA.","Saying C'È for past — past needs C'ERA."]},"dialogue":[{"sp":"Sofia","t":"Com'era il tempo ieri?","r":"koh-MEH-rah eel TEHM-poh YEH-ree?","en":"How was the weather yesterday?"},{"sp":"Marco","t":"Faceva bello. C'era il sole.","r":"fah-CHEH-vah BEHL-loh. CHEH-rah eel SOH-leh.","en":"It was nice. There was sun."},{"sp":"Sofia","t":"E oggi?","r":"eh OHD-jee?","en":"And today?"},{"sp":"Marco","t":"Piove!","r":"PYOH-veh!","en":"It rains!"}],"practice":[{"type":"translate_en","q":"Say: It was nice","answer":"Faceva bello"},{"type":"fill","q":"C'era ___ (wind)","answer":"vento"},{"type":"choose","q":"'There was sun' is…","options":["C'è il sole","C'era il sole","Faceva sole","È sole"],"answer":"C'era il sole"},{"type":"reorder","q":"Order: bello / faceva","answer":"faceva bello"},{"type":"speak","q":"Say aloud: Faceva bello.","answer":"Faceva bello."}],"quiz":[{"q":"FACEVA BELLO means…","options":["it is nice","it was nice","it will rain","it snowed"],"answer":1,"why":"Faceva = was (imperfetto)."},{"q":"LA PIOGGIA is…","options":["sun","rain","wind","cloud"],"answer":1,"why":"Pioggia = rain."},{"q":"C'ERA VENTO means…","options":["it is windy","there was wind","wind comes","no wind"],"answer":1,"why":"C'era = there was."},{"q":"Weather in the past uses…","options":["passato prossimo","imperfetto","future","present"],"answer":1,"why":"Scenes = imperfetto."},{"q":"COM'ERA IL TEMPO? asks…","options":["what time was it?","how was the weather?","where was he?","who came?"],"answer":1,"why":"Tempo = weather (also time!)."}],"flashcards":"auto:vocab","worksheet":{"title":"Weather worksheet","tasks":[{"instruction":"Translate to Italian.","items":["sun","rain","winter"],"key":["il sole","la pioggia","l'inverno"]},{"instruction":"Paint past skies.","items":["It was nice","There was wind","It was cold yesterday"],"key":["Faceva bello","C'era vento","Faceva freddo ieri"]},{"instruction":"Talk weather.","items":["How was the weather yesterday?","And today?"],"key":["Com'era il tempo ieri?","E oggi?"]}]}}]}],"test":{"title":"A2 final test","items":[{"type":"translate_en","q":"Say: Where is the station?","answer":"Dov'è la stazione?"},{"type":"fill","q":"Vado ___ Roma (to)","answer":"a"},{"type":"choose","q":"'I get up at seven'","options":["Alzo alle sette","Mi alzo alle sette","Si alza alle sette","Ti alzi alle sette"],"answer":"Mi alzo alle sette"},{"type":"translate_en","q":"Say: I leave tomorrow","answer":"Parto domani"},{"type":"translate_t","q":"Mi fa male la testa.","answer":"My head hurts."},{"type":"fill","q":"È ___ (near)","answer":"vicino"},{"type":"reorder","q":"Order: piaciuto / è / ti / ?","answer":"ti è piaciuto?"},{"type":"speak","q":"Say aloud: Dov'è la banca?","answer":"Dov'è la banca?"},{"type":"fill","q":"___ bello. (it was nice)","answer":"Faceva"},{"type":"choose","q":"'This shirt is cheap'","options":["Questo camicia è economica","Questa camicia è economica","Queste camicia sono economiche","Questa camicia economica è"],"answer":"Questa camicia è economica"}]}}}